# A git worktree here holds a COMPLETE second copy of this repository, so an
# unqualified `git add -A` would commit the tree into itself. Machine-local
# settings are local by their own name. Neither is the project.
#
# .prettierignore excludes the same directory for the same reason (issues.md
# I-20); this is the other half of it (I-21). Nothing else under .claude/ is
# ignored, so a config the maker decides to track stays visible.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
